            </tr>
            <tr style="height:176.7000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Course Schedule (Please supply the details about each lesson with 96 academic hours in a total of 16 weeks):<strong> </strong></p>
<p>Week&nbsp; 1-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Introduction, description of osteology & arthrology; bones of trunk</p>
<p>&nbsp; 1-2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The articulation of trunk bones, cranial bones & their articulation</p>
<p>Week&nbsp; 2-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Upper limb bones & their articulation</p>
<p>&nbsp; 2-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Lower limb bones & their articulation</p>
<p>Week&nbsp; 3-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Introduction of myology muscles of head, neck & trunk</p>
<p>&nbsp; 3-2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Muscles of trunk & muscle of upper limb</p>
<p>Week&nbsp; 4-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Muscles of upper limb & lower limb</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;4-2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; General introduction of splanchnology, digestive system</p>
<p>Week&nbsp;&nbsp; 5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; National day</p>
<p>Week&nbsp; 6-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Respiratory system</p>
<p>&nbsp; 6-2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Urinary system & Male reproductive system</p>
<p>Week&nbsp; 7-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Male & Female reproductive systems</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;7-2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Introduction to Circulatory system & Heart</p>
<p>Week&nbsp; 8-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Heart & Artery (part 1)</p>
<p>&nbsp;8-2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Arteries (part 2)</p>
<p>Week&nbsp; 9-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Veins</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;9-2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Lymphatic system</p>
<p>Week 10-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Sensory organs-Visual organs</p>
<p>&nbsp; 10-2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Sensory organs-Vestibulocochlear organ</p>
<p>Week&nbsp; 11-1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; General introduction of nervous system; Spinal nerve（part 1）</p>
<p>&nbsp;11-2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Spinal nerve（part 2）</p>
